            {
              "id": "b929b2fb-6bb7-3248-b9a3-25d5dd534f06",
              "name": "Bcrypt Hash Vulnerability Detected",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Bcrypt Hash Vulnerability Detected\" vulnerability in JavaScript refers to the situation where a weak or default bcrypt hash is used for password hashing. Bcrypt is a password hashing function designed by Niels Provos and David Mazières, based on the Blowfish cipher. The bcrypt function is the default password hash algorithm for BSD and other systems. The prefix \"$2b$\" (or \"2y\") in a hash string in a shadow password file indicates that hash string is a bcrypt hash in modular crypt format.\n\nThe vulnerability arises when the bcrypt hash is not strong enough (i.e., the cost factor is too low) or when a default hash is used, which can be easily cracked by attackers.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Use a strong bcrypt hash with a high cost factor. The cost factor is the logarithmic iteration count used in the bcrypt hash algorithm. The higher the cost factor, the more secure the hash, but also the more processing power required to validate passwords against it.\n\n2. Avoid using default bcrypt hashes. Always generate a new bcrypt hash for each user password.\n\n3. Regularly update and rehash user passwords.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe following is a JavaScript code example using the `bcrypt` library to generate a strong bcrypt hash:\n\n```javascript\nconst bcrypt = require('bcrypt');\nconst saltRounds = 12; // Increase the cost factor to 12\n\nbcrypt.hash('myPassword', saltRounds, function(err, hash) {\n  // Store hash in your password DB.\n});\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library:\n\n- bcrypt: A library to help you hash passwords.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Password Storage Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Password_Storage_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-916: Use of Password Hash With Insufficient Computational Effort](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/916.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-916",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/916.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
