            {
              "id": "af71c4dd-c8d9-3e9e-a5c2-69bf3050cf99",
              "name": "\"High-Risk Vulnerability in Cross-Spawn Package: Update to Fixed Versions for Mitigation\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `cross-spawn` package is a popular npm package used for spawning child processes in a way that works across all platforms. A high-risk vulnerability has been identified in version 7.0.3 of the `cross-spawn` package. This vulnerability could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the server where the application is running, leading to serious security concerns such as data breaches, unauthorized access, and system compromise.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThe vulnerability in the `cross-spawn` package is a security concern because it can be exploited by an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the server. This could potentially lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, disruption of the application's functionality, or even complete system compromise. The severity of the impact depends on the privileges of the user running the application and the nature of the operations performed by the application.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to update the `cross-spawn` package to a version where the vulnerability has been fixed. Regularly updating all dependencies to their latest stable versions is a good practice to prevent similar vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nUpdate the `cross-spawn` package to the latest version by modifying the `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"cross-spawn\": \"^latest\"\n```\n\nThen, run `npm update` to update the package.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe `cross-spawn` package requires the following dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `path-key`: \"^3.1.0\"\n- `shebang-command`: \"^2.0.0\"\n- `which`: \"^2.0.1\"\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/)\n\nPlease note that the specific CWE for this vulnerability may vary depending on the nature of the vulnerability. It is recommended to refer to the vulnerability report for the specific CWE."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [],
                "severity": "HIGH",
                "kind": "FAIL"
              }
