            {
              "id": "6c73490a-8ccd-30ee-883c-0670dc70a8d8",
              "name": "\"High-Risk Vulnerability in Node-Forge Package Version 1.3.1, Resolved in Version 1.3.2 (CVE-2025-12816)\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "**Description**\n\nThe Node-Forge package version 1.3.1 has a high-risk vulnerability (CVE-2025-12816) that has been resolved in version 1.3.2. Node-Forge is a native implementation of Transport Layer Security in pure JavaScript and it is used by Docker programming language. The vulnerability in question could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service through a crafted certificate.\n\n**Security Concern**\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code in the context of the application. This could lead to unauthorized access, data corruption or even a complete system compromise. Additionally, the vulnerability could be exploited to cause a denial of service, rendering the application unavailable to legitimate users.\n\n**Mitigation Advice**\n\nThe best way to mitigate this vulnerability is to update the Node-Forge package to version 1.3.2 or later. This can be done by modifying the package.json file in your project to specify the updated version:\n\n```json\n\"node-forge\": {\n  \"version\": \"1.3.2\",\n  \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/node-forge/-/node-forge-1.3.2.tgz\",\n  \"integrity\": \"sha512-...\"\n}\n```\n\nThen, run `npm install` to update the package.\n\n**Library Dependencies**\n\nThe Node-Forge package does not have any other library dependencies.\n\n**OWASP and CWE Resources**\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are valid and active for anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-94",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "HIGH",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-94"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
