            {
              "id": "8971dd62-eab7-3b5c-ab35-06ede3be59e2",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in Path-to-Regexp Package Version 1.8.0, Fixed in Versions 1.9.0, 0.1.10, 8.0.0, 3.3.0, 6.3.0 (CVE-2024-45296)\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `path-to-regexp` package version 1.8.0 in Docker programming language has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2024-45296). This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code due to improper input validation. This is a security concern as it can lead to unauthorized access, data corruption, and potential system takeover.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `path-to-regexp` package to versions 1.9.0, 0.1.10, 8.0.0, 3.3.0, or 6.3.0 which contain the fix for this vulnerability. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nUpdate the `path-to-regexp` package in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"path-to-regexp\": {\n  \"version\": \"1.9.0\",\n  \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/path-to-regexp/-/path-to-regexp-1.9.0.tgz\",\n  \"integrity\": \"sha512-...\",\n  \"requires\": {\n    \"isarray\": \"0.0.1\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `isarray` version 0.0.1\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 - A1 Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A1_2017-Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
