            {
              "id": "baa037f4-421e-36fa-a321-5b3501f0d676",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in nth-check Package, Resolved in Version 2.0.1 (CVE-2021-3803)\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `nth-check` package is a JavaScript library that is used to parse and compile CSS selector strings. A high severity vulnerability (CVE-2021-3803) was discovered in versions prior to 2.0.1. This vulnerability is a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) issue, which can cause the application to consume excessive system resources, leading to a denial of service.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nA ReDoS attack can cause an application to consume excessive system resources by providing a malicious input that triggers a worst-case scenario for a regular expression. This can lead to the application becoming unresponsive or slow, impacting its availability and potentially causing a denial of service. In a worst-case scenario, this could be exploited to cause a complete system shutdown.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nThe vulnerability has been fixed in version 2.0.1 of the `nth-check` package. Therefore, the recommended mitigation is to update the `nth-check` package to version 2.0.1 or later. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nUpdate the `nth-check` package in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"nth-check\": {\n  \"version\": \"2.0.1\",\n  \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/nth-check/-/nth-check-2.0.1.tgz\",\n  \"integrity\": \"sha512-WeBOdju8SnzPN5vTUJYxYUxLeXpCaVP5i5e0LF8fg7WORF2Wd7wFX/pk0tYZk7s8T+J7VLy0Da6J1+wCT0AtHg==\",\n  \"requires\": {\n    \"boolbase\": \"~1.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe `nth-check` package requires the `boolbase` package version ~1.0.0.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP ReDoS](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Regular_expression_Denial_of_Service_-_ReDoS)\n- [CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)"
              },
