              "name": "\"High-Risk Vulnerability in Rollup Package, Resolved in Later Versions\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability in question is related to the `rollup` package version `2.79.1` used in Docker programming. The `rollup` package is a module bundler for JavaScript which compiles small pieces of code into something larger and more complex, such as a library or application. \n\nThe high-risk vulnerability in this version of the package could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code, leading to unauthorized access or control over the system. This is a significant security concern as it could lead to data breaches, system crashes, or other malicious activities.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `rollup` package to a later version where the vulnerability has been resolved. Regularly updating and patching software is a key aspect of maintaining secure systems. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix this vulnerability in the source code, you need to update the `rollup` package to the latest version. You can do this by running the following command:\n\n```bash\nnpm install rollup@latest\n```\n\nThis will update the `rollup` package to the latest version, mitigating the vulnerability.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `fsevents` version `~2.3.2`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are valid and active for anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
