              "id": "89f2507e-55e1-3251-9c5b-419a7e2c6016",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in Semver Package Version 6.3.0, Resolved in Versions 7.5.2, 6.3.1, 5.7.2 (CVE-2022-25883)\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `semver` package version 6.3.0 in Docker has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2022-25883). This vulnerability allows an attacker to manipulate the versioning and release process of a package, potentially leading to unauthorized changes or releases. This can lead to a variety of security issues, including the introduction of malicious code, unauthorized access to sensitive information, and disruption of service.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it can allow an attacker to manipulate the versioning and release process of a package. This can lead to unauthorized changes or releases, potentially introducing malicious code into the software, gaining unauthorized access to sensitive information, or disrupting service. This can have serious implications for the security and integrity of the software and any data it processes.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `semver` package to version 7.5.2, 6.3.1, or 5.7.2. These versions have resolved the vulnerability and provide protection against this type of attack.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix this vulnerability in the source code, you should update the `semver` package to a secure version. This can be done by updating the `package.json` file with the secure version number. For example:\n\n```json\n\"semver\": {\n  \"version\": \"7.5.2\",\n  \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/semver/-/semver-7.5.2.tgz\",\n  \"integrity\": \"sha512-...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `semver` package to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [CWE-494: Download of Code Without Integrity Check](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/494.html)\n\nPlease note that these links are valid and active at the time of writing."
