              "id": "41a13339-0fde-3905-98f0-9fc8f7640e77",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in Semver Package Version 7.5.1, Resolved in Versions 7.5.2, 6.3.1, 5.7.2 (CVE-2022-25883)\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe Semver package version 7.5.1 has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2022-25883). This vulnerability is a security concern because it allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code remotely. This can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, disruption of service, and potentially taking control of the affected system.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the Semver package to versions 7.5.2, 6.3.1, or 5.7.2 where the vulnerability has been resolved. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn your `package.json` file, update the version of Semver:\n\n```json\n\"semver\": \"^7.5.2\"\n```\n\nThen, run `npm install` to update your dependencies.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- semver: 7.5.1\n- lru-cache: 6.0.0\n- yallist: 4.0.0\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/index.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are valid and active for anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
