                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `path-to-regexp` package version 0.1.7 has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2024-52798). This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code due to improper input validation. This is a security concern as it can lead to unauthorized access, data corruption, and potential system compromise.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `path-to-regexp` package to version 0.1.12 or later. This version contains a fix for the vulnerability.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix the vulnerability in the source code, you need to update the `path-to-regexp` package in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"path-to-regexp\": {\n  \"version\": \"0.1.12\",\n  \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/path-to-regexp/-/path-to-regexp-0.1.12.tgz\",\n  \"integrity\": \"sha512-5DFkuoqlv1uYQKxy8omFBeJPQcdoE07Kv2sferDCrAq1ohOU+MSDswDIbnx3YAM60qIOnYa53wBhXW0EbMonrQ==\"\n}\n```\n\nThen, run `npm install` to update the package.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `path-to-regexp` package to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are valid and active for anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
