              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `ws` package version 7.5.9 in Docker has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2024-37890). This vulnerability is a security concern as it could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code, leading to unauthorized access or control of the system.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it could allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the system where the Docker container is running. This could lead to unauthorized access or control of the system, data leakage, or even a denial of service (DoS) attack. \n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `ws` package to a secure version. The vulnerability has been resolved in versions 5.2.4, 6.2.3, 7.5.10, 8.17.1. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix the vulnerability in the source code, you should update the `ws` package version in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"ws\": {\n  \"version\": \"7.5.10\",\n  \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/ws/-/ws-7.5.10.tgz\",\n  \"integrity\": \"sha512-...\"\n}\n```\n\nThen, run `npm install` to install the updated package.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `ws` package to execute properly.\n\n## Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/index.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are valid and active for anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
