              "id": "5af70a70-ec57-329c-a6da-3ec7fba3fd1c",
              "name": "Potential Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) Vulnerability Detected in Anchor Tag 'href' Attribute",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) is a type of security vulnerability that enables attackers to inject malicious scripts into web pages viewed by other users. In this case, the vulnerability is detected in the 'href' attribute of an anchor tag. The `book._id` parameter in the `Link` component is directly used to construct the URL, which can potentially lead to an XSS attack if the `book._id` is not properly sanitized and contains malicious scripts.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always sanitize and validate user inputs. Never trust user inputs blindly. In this case, you should ensure that `book._id` is properly sanitized before using it to construct the URL.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```jsx\nimport React from 'react';\nimport { Link } from 'react-router-dom';\nimport sanitizeHtml from 'sanitize-html';\n\nconst content = book => {\n    const sanitizedId = sanitizeHtml(book._id);\n    return (\n        <Link to={`/books/${sanitizedId}`}>\n            <button className=\"btn btn-primary btn-sm\">Update</button>\n        </Link>\n    );\n};\n```\n\nIn the above code, we use the `sanitize-html` library to sanitize `book._id` before using it.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n- react\n- react-router-dom\n- sanitize-html\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
