            {
              "id": "8adadd0e-811f-3668-927d-9755b45b4e2e",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when data enters a program from an untrusted source and is used to generate dynamic HTML content. The vulnerability in the provided code snippet arises from the use of user-controlled data (`book._id`) in an HTML string without proper sanitization or encoding. This could potentially allow an attacker to inject malicious scripts into the web page, which would then be executed in the browser of any user viewing that page.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always encode user-controlled data before including it in HTML. This can be done using JavaScript's built-in encoding functions or third-party libraries. Additionally, you should use a Content Security Policy (CSP) to restrict the sources from which scripts can be loaded, and to disable inline scripts.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn this specific case, you can use the `encodeURIComponent` function to encode the `book._id` before including it in the URL:\n\n```jsx\ncontent: book => (\n    <Link to={`/books/${encodeURIComponent(book._id)}`}>\n        <button className=\"btn btn-primary btn-sm\">Update</button>\n    </Link>\n)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet appears to be using the following libraries:\n\n- React (for the JSX syntax and the `Link` component)\n- react-router-dom (for the `Link` component)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Content Security Policy Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Content_Security_Policy_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
