            {
              "id": "c7f108bd-a185-36ea-9331-e47af6e88aa2",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability Detected through `ref` Usage\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. XSS allows attackers to execute scripts in the victim's browser which can hijack user sessions, deface web sites, or redirect the user to malicious sites.\n\nIn the context of ReactJS, using `ref` attribute can potentially lead to XSS vulnerabilities if the reference is used to directly manipulate the DOM with untrusted user input. In the provided code snippet:\n\n```jsx\n<NotificationSystem ref={this.notificationSystem} />\n```\n\nIf `this.notificationSystem` is influenced by user input, it could lead to a potential XSS vulnerability.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate potential XSS vulnerabilities in ReactJS:\n\n1. Avoid using `ref` to directly manipulate the DOM with user input.\n2. Always sanitize user input, even if it is not directly inserted into the DOM.\n3. Use React's built-in protection against XSS. React escapes all variable content by default, so unless you're using `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` or manipulating the DOM with `ref`, you're protected.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nAssuming `this.notificationSystem` is a callback function that is used to store a reference to the DOM node, you should ensure that it does not use any user-supplied input to manipulate the DOM. A safe usage of `ref` would look like this:\n\n```jsx\n<NotificationSystem ref={notificationSystem => this.notificationSystem = notificationSystem} />\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `react`\n- `react-dom`\n- `react-notification-system` (assuming `NotificationSystem` is a component from this library)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP DOM based XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/DOM_based_XSS_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
