              "id": "a3187ee1-7ba0-3fd7-8af9-e37ed8537419",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in jws Package Version 3.2.2, Resolved in Versions 3.2.3 and 4.0.1\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `jws` package version 3.2.2 has a high severity vulnerability. This vulnerability is a security concern because it can potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code, leading to unauthorized access or control of the system. This vulnerability has been resolved in versions 3.2.3 and 4.0.1 of the `jws` package.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThe vulnerability in the `jws` package version 3.2.2 can be exploited by an attacker to execute arbitrary code. This can lead to unauthorized access or control of the system, potentially compromising sensitive data or disrupting system operations. \n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to update the `jws` package to version 3.2.3 or 4.0.1. This can be done by running the following command:\n\n```bash\nnpm install jws@3.2.3\n```\nor\n```bash\nnpm install jws@4.0.1\n```\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn your `package.json` file, update the `jws` version in the dependencies section:\n\n```json\n\"dependencies\": {\n  \"jws\": \"^3.2.3\",\n  \"jwa\": \"^1.4.1\",\n  \"safe-buffer\": \"^5.0.1\"\n}\n```\nor\n```json\n\"dependencies\": {\n  \"jws\": \"^4.0.1\",\n  \"jwa\": \"^1.4.1\",\n  \"safe-buffer\": \"^5.0.1\"\n}\n```\nThen run `npm install` to update your dependencies.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `jws` version 3.2.3 or 4.0.1\n- `jwa` version ^1.4.1\n- `safe-buffer` version ^5.0.1\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 Security Risks](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/)\n\nPlease note that the specific CWE for this vulnerability is not mentioned, but it may fall under [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html) or [CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)."
