              "id": "1fe34402-a72a-3a37-8f28-14a1a4161873",
              "name": "High-Risk Vulnerability in Webpack-Dev-Middleware Package: CVE-2024-29180, Fixed in Versions 7.1.0, 6.1.2, 5.3.4",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability CVE-2024-29180 is a high-risk vulnerability found in the `webpack-dev-middleware` package versions prior to 7.1.0, 6.1.2, and 5.3.4. This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the server where the package is running. This is a serious security concern as it can lead to unauthorized access and control over the server, potentially leading to data theft, data corruption, or denial of service.\n\n## Mitigation\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to update the `webpack-dev-middleware` package to versions 7.1.0, 6.1.2, or 5.3.4 or later. If updating is not an option, consider using a virtual private network (VPN) or firewall to restrict access to the server.\n\n## Code Fix\n\nUpdate the `webpack-dev-middleware` package in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"webpack-dev-middleware\": \"^7.1.0\"\n```\n\nThen run `npm update` to update your packages.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe `webpack-dev-middleware` package requires the following dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- colorette: ^2.0.10\n- memfs: ^3.4.3\n- mime-types: ^2.1.31\n- range-parser: ^1.2.1\n- schema-utils: ^4.0.0\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/)\n- [CVE-2024-29180](https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2024-29180)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are valid and active for anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
