              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "**Description**\n\nThe `ws` package version `8.13.0` has a high severity vulnerability, identified as `CVE-2024-37890`. This vulnerability allows for potential Denial of Service (DoS) attacks. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to cause the application to crash, making it unavailable to users.\n\n**Security Concern**\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it can be exploited to make the application unavailable, affecting its availability aspect of the CIA triad (Confidentiality, Integrity, and Availability). This could lead to loss of service for legitimate users and potential business impact.\n\n**Mitigation Advice**\n\nThe vulnerability has been resolved in versions `5.2.4`, `6.2.3`, `7.5.10`, and `8.17.1` of the `ws` package. It is recommended to update your `ws` package to one of these versions or later to mitigate this vulnerability.\n\n**Source Code Fix Recommendation**\n\nUpdate the `ws` package in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"dependencies\": {\n  \"ws\": \"^8.17.1\"\n}\n```\n\nThen run `npm install` to update your dependencies.\n\n**Library Dependencies**\n\nThe code example requires the `ws` package to execute properly.\n\n**OWASP and CWE Resources**\n\n- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
