              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe Mongoose package vulnerability CVE-2024-53900 is a hypothetical vulnerability (as the CVE number suggests a future date and there is no official record of this specific CVE at the time of writing) that could potentially affect the Mongoose package in Docker programming language. The vulnerability is resolved in versions 8.8.3, 7.8.3, and 6.13.5 of the Mongoose package.\n\nThis vulnerability could be a security concern as it might allow an attacker to exploit the system by manipulating the Mongoose package, leading to unauthorized access, data corruption, or even a system crash.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to update the Mongoose package to the latest version or at least to the versions where the vulnerability has been resolved (8.8.3, 7.8.3, 6.13.5).\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nUpdate the Mongoose package version in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"dependencies\": {\n  \"mongoose\": \"^8.8.3\"\n}\n```\n\nThen, run `npm install` to update the package.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- bson: ^5.3.0\n- kareem: 2.5.1\n- mongodb: 5.5.0\n- mpath: 0.9.0\n- mquery: 5.0.0\n- ms: 2.1.3\n- sift: 16.0.1\n\n## Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/)\n\nPlease note that the actual vulnerability and its details might differ as the provided CVE number is hypothetical and does not correspond to a known vulnerability at the time of writing."
