              "id": "713b800f-4241-31d4-a177-99237849ec40",
              "name": "\"High Severity Vulnerability in Path-to-Regexp Package Version 0.1.7, Fixed in Version 0.1.12 (CVE-2024-52798)\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `path-to-regexp` package version 0.1.7 has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2024-52798). This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code due to insufficient input validation. This can lead to serious security issues such as data breaches, unauthorized access, and system crashes.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThis vulnerability is a security concern because it allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code in the context of the application. This can lead to a variety of security issues, including unauthorized access to sensitive data, disruption of service, and potentially even full system compromise.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `path-to-regexp` package to version 0.1.12 or later. This version includes a fix for the vulnerability.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix the vulnerability in the source code, you should update the `path-to-regexp` package in your `package.json` file:\n\n```json\n\"dependencies\": {\n  \"path-to-regexp\": \"^0.1.12\"\n}\n```\n\nThen, run `npm install` to update the package.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `path-to-regexp` package to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 Security Risks](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Node.js Security Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that all links were active and working for anonymous users at the time of writing."
