                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `qs` package version 6.11.0 in Docker programming language has a high severity vulnerability (CVE-2025-15284). This vulnerability is a security concern as it allows attackers to execute arbitrary code remotely, leading to unauthorized access and potential data breaches.\n\n## Security Concern\n\nThe vulnerability in the `qs` package is a security concern because it can be exploited by attackers to execute arbitrary code remotely. This can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive data, disruption of services, and potential data breaches. The vulnerability can be exploited if an attacker sends a specially crafted request to the application using the `qs` package.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to upgrade the `qs` package to version 6.14.1 or later. This version has resolved the vulnerability and provides improved security. Regularly updating and patching your software can help prevent such vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo fix the vulnerability in the source code, you need to update the `qs` package to version 6.14.1 or later. You can do this by running the following command:\n\n```bash\nnpm update qs@6.14.1\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `side-channel` version 1.0.4 or later\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)](https://cwe.mitre.org/)\n\nPlease note that these links are valid and active at the time of writing this report."
